                    Design: We propose to improve                               
                    optimization and regularization by                          
                    switching to the AdamW optimizer with                       
                    weight decay and adding a cosine                            
                    annealing learning‐rate scheduler. This                     
                    scheduler will gradually decrease the                       
                    learning rate to help the model                             
                    converge smoothly and potentially                           
                    escape local minima, yielding better                        
                    generalization. We keep the existing                        
                    MixUp augmentation and EfficientNet‐B0                      
                    backbone but now train with AdamW                           
                    (weight decay=1e‐2) and step the                            
                    scheduler each epoch. The rest of the                       
                    training and evaluation pipeline                            
                    remains unchanged.                                          
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without errors. The model                      
                    was trained for 5 epochs using MixUp                        
                    augmentation and cosine annealing                           
