                    Design: We will enhance the training                        
                    data augmentation by injecting random                       
                    color jitter—varying brightness,                            
                    contrast, saturation, and hue—to better                     
                    simulate real‐world lighting variations                     
                    and improve generalization.                                 
                    Specifically, we add                                        
                    T.ColorJitter(brightness=0.2,                               
                    contrast=0.2, saturation=0.2, hue=0.1)                      
                    into the existing train_transform                           
                    pipeline. Everything else remains                           
                    unchanged, including the                                    
                    EfficientNet‐B0 backbone, MixUp, and                        
                    multi‐view test‐time augmentation. We                       
                    will train for 5 epochs, evaluate                           
                    validation AUROC, and produce a                             
                    submission.csv for any test images.                         
